WEBVTT

00:05.130 --> 00:07.230
<i>My name is Valefor.</i>

00:07.540 --> 00:10.410
<i>I thought I would never  
 write in this diary again,</i>

00:10.410 --> 00:12.360
<i>but I find myself back in this castle.</i>

00:12.810 --> 00:14.800
<i>I'm doing well.</i>

00:15.260 --> 00:17.970
<i>I wasn't able to run away 
from home for very long.</i>

00:17.970 --> 00:20.040
<i>It seems there's no escaping an Archdemon.</i>

00:20.690 --> 00:23.330
<i>I almost want to tear out 
the last page I wrote,</i>

00:23.330 --> 00:25.790
<i>but I'm going to leave it 
as a reminder to myself.</i>

00:26.290 --> 00:30.670
<i>When Zagan came to my rescue, 
shameful as it is to admit, I was relieved.</i>

00:31.040 --> 00:34.430
<i>He and Nephy protected me.</i>

00:34.850 --> 00:37.930
<i>Not only them, but the man who 
I thought killed my father, too.</i>

00:38.400 --> 00:42.480
<i>I should also mention that Tail-Head 
helped, as strange as that sounds.</i>

00:43.040 --> 00:44.810
I think she did, anyway.

00:45.290 --> 00:48.840
<i>I don't yet know what 
I can do to repay them all.</i>

00:48.840 --> 00:51.470
<i>But I want to show my 
gratitude, a bit at a time.</i>

00:51.470 --> 00:54.630
<i>And to do that, I'll need to become strong.</i>

00:54.630 --> 00:56.110
<i>That's what my goal is.</i>

00:56.530 --> 01:00.200
<i>And I'm going to continue this 
diary for the time being.</i>

01:01.010 --> 01:03.910
<i>I think that I'll write about the 
newest member of the household.</i>

01:04.280 --> 01:06.090
<i>His name is Raphael.</i>

01:06.090 --> 01:08.550
<i>He wields one of those 
wretched Sacred Swords,</i>

01:08.550 --> 01:10.830
<i>and I thought he had killed my father,</i>

01:10.830 --> 01:16.930
<i>but he actually respected my father a
 great deal, and lost his arm protecting me.</i>

01:17.990 --> 01:22.350
<i>I still don't know how to 
feel about him, to be honest.</i>

01:22.930 --> 01:25.640
<i>Raphael's cooking is delicious.</i>

01:25.640 --> 01:31.140
<i>He's a good match for Nephy in that regard, 
but he knows a much wider variety of sweets.</i>

01:31.140 --> 01:34.740
<i>And he always lets me try 
the things he makes first.</i>

01:35.380 --> 01:37.740
<i>I do have one problem with him.</i>

01:37.740 --> 01:41.990
<i>Whenever I'm trying to observe Zagan 
and Nephy's couple activities,</i>

01:41.990 --> 01:43.830
<i>he tries to get in my way.</i>

01:44.340 --> 01:47.710
<i>It's become a source of 
consistent conflict between us.</i>

01:47.990 --> 01:49.540
<i>Today, for example...</i>

01:49.860 --> 01:52.940
Mr. Raphael taught me this recipe.

01:52.940 --> 01:54.590
These are a confection called macarons.

01:54.590 --> 01:56.170
I helped!

01:56.430 --> 01:57.620
I see.

01:57.620 --> 01:59.550
They certainly look cute.

01:59.550 --> 02:03.120
The name is apparently taken from 
the type of pasta called "macaroni."

02:03.120 --> 02:04.920
They're completely different dishes,

02:04.920 --> 02:07.480
but the method for making 
them has something in common.

02:07.930 --> 02:11.580
The ancient sorcerer known as the 
King of Feasts, Caesar Cardia,

02:11.580 --> 02:14.190
had an apprentice named 
Nancy de Lorraine who conceived of it.

02:15.410 --> 02:18.640
You're rather well-informed on
 sorcerous cooking for an Angelic Knight.

02:18.640 --> 02:20.200
Begging your pardon, sir.

02:20.540 --> 02:22.710
So... how do you eat one?

02:22.710 --> 02:25.640
You just take it with your hand and eat it.

02:25.640 --> 02:26.570
I see.

02:26.570 --> 02:31.830
Oh, Lord Zagan, these sweets are very 
delicate, so be gentle when picking it up.

02:32.880 --> 02:34.330
Gently, eh?

02:39.470 --> 02:41.550
Nephy! Take up the dessert!

02:43.590 --> 02:45.680
When you say that...

02:47.250 --> 02:48.430
No, never mind.

02:49.740 --> 02:51.440
No! I'll pick it up!

03:02.840 --> 03:06.330
<i>That was when he started hiding his 
presence and snuck up behind me.</i>

03:06.330 --> 03:08.540
<i>It wasn't the kind of thing 
just anyone could pull off.</i>

03:08.940 --> 03:11.460
<i>I was able to dodge quickly enough.</i>

03:11.460 --> 03:17.340
<i>That wasn't easy, either, since I was trying 
to make sure Zagan and Nephy didn't notice.</i>

03:19.720 --> 03:21.740
<i>I won that time.</i>

03:21.740 --> 03:25.350
<i>My reward was a nice, toasty 
sensation inside of my chest.</i>

03:25.740 --> 03:28.270
Wh-What do you think, Lord Zagan?

03:28.270 --> 03:30.100
It's a big world out there.

03:30.100 --> 03:32.350
I had no idea food with this 
kind of texture existed.

03:32.670 --> 03:36.080
The outside is crispy,
 but the inside is creamy.

03:36.080 --> 03:37.360
And it's incredibly sweet.

03:37.750 --> 03:41.450
Would you like one Nephy? 
This time, I'll hold it for you.

03:44.850 --> 03:46.590
Why are you getting in the way?

03:46.590 --> 03:49.770
I told you before, you're still 
too young for this sort of thing.

03:49.770 --> 03:51.880
I don't really see how.

03:52.800 --> 03:56.030
It's obvious how those two 
barely even hold hands.

03:56.030 --> 03:59.880
Can you imagine how many 
decades it'll be before they kiss?

04:01.570 --> 04:03.440
H-Here I come, Nephy.

04:03.440 --> 04:04.720
R-Right!

04:07.210 --> 04:10.400
<i>If we're noticed, then it's a mutual defeat.</i>

04:10.400 --> 04:14.100
<i>Neither Raphael nor 
I want to interrupt them.</i>

04:14.390 --> 04:19.500
<i>It's my intention to ultimately come 
out on top in this battle, however.</i>

04:19.500 --> 04:21.960
For, it's time to go!

04:21.960 --> 04:24.110
Okay! Coming.

04:24.390 --> 04:28.370
<i>Additionally, Tail-Head is coming 
over to spend the night today.</i>

04:28.370 --> 04:31.470
<i>Nephy is excited about 
cooking a feast for her,</i>

04:31.470 --> 04:33.450
<i>so we're going into town to shop.</i>

06:03.960 --> 06:08.970
<b>Episode 12: 
Music At Night Is Lovely, But May Be 
Too Much When You're Socially Awkward</b>

06:17.480 --> 06:19.250
Hey, it's the Archdemon.

06:19.250 --> 06:22.770
Yeah. His wife's a beauty, 
and his daughter's adorable, too.

06:23.520 --> 06:26.900
The three of them are always together lately.
 They must be getting along.

06:28.480 --> 06:31.240
<i>Nephy has really made herself 
at home in town.</i>

06:35.490 --> 06:37.390
Is there anything else we need?

06:37.390 --> 06:39.440
No, that should be everything.

06:39.440 --> 06:43.710
Oh, but is it all right if we stop 
by Miss Manuela's store for a bit?

06:44.990 --> 06:47.970
<i>That's always a recipe for trouble.</i>

06:52.170 --> 06:54.970
You made these, Nephy?! That's awesome!

06:54.970 --> 06:58.060
I wanted to repay you for 
teaching me so many recipes.

06:58.300 --> 07:01.890
Thank you so much! 
You're such an enthusiastic student!

07:01.890 --> 07:06.540
Oh, we just got some new stock in.
 Let's have you try them on!

07:06.540 --> 07:08.070
There are ones that For can try, too!

07:08.340 --> 07:12.280
We actually don't have much 
time today... Maybe next time.

07:12.280 --> 07:13.900
Aw, really?

07:13.900 --> 07:15.710
Then we had better do this fast.

07:15.710 --> 07:18.120
Leave it to me! Come on!

07:18.980 --> 07:20.480
Right this way.

07:20.480 --> 07:21.370
It won't take long!

07:20.480 --> 07:21.370
Hey!

07:21.730 --> 07:23.570
<i>This is what I was worried about.</i>

07:27.060 --> 07:29.210
Well, you don't see one of these every day.

07:29.510 --> 07:31.300
Oh, that thing?

07:31.730 --> 07:33.190
What is it?

07:33.190 --> 07:35.970
It's called a phonograph.
 You use it to listen to music.

07:36.430 --> 07:39.770
There's actually a variety of sorcerers 
who deal with sounds and music.

07:40.220 --> 07:43.800
This was created by one such ancient 
sorcerer, named Victor One,

07:43.800 --> 07:46.320
the Aural Count, who had a 
fixation on quality of sound.

07:46.880 --> 07:50.490
This definitely looks like an antique.

07:50.490 --> 07:52.850
Probably held on to by some eccentric.

07:53.690 --> 07:55.450
So it plays music?

07:55.790 --> 07:58.740
It's actually broken, so it can't.

07:59.080 --> 08:00.520
I can tell.

08:00.520 --> 08:05.000
Some of the street kids found 
it and were hoping to sell it.

08:06.750 --> 08:10.010
But none of the stores were interested,

08:10.010 --> 08:11.800
so they ended up leaving it here.

08:18.090 --> 08:19.650
<i>Street urchins, huh...</i>

08:19.650 --> 08:23.270
<i>I remember we snatched up anything 
we thought might sell, too.</i>

08:42.380 --> 08:44.370
I'm going to buy this phonograph.

08:48.880 --> 08:50.880
But this is so much...

08:50.880 --> 08:53.960
Enough to buy hundreds of 
outfits for those kids.

08:53.960 --> 08:55.670
This is how much it's supposed to cost.

08:55.670 --> 08:57.340
The cash is yours to do with as you like.

08:57.680 --> 08:59.600
It's broken, though.

08:59.890 --> 09:02.120
Come on. It's a simple enough sorcerous tool.

09:02.120 --> 09:04.020
I'll be able to fix it easily.

09:04.020 --> 09:09.020
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

09:13.440 --> 09:15.240
I guess we're early.

09:15.560 --> 09:17.790
Oh, they'll be back shortly.

09:17.790 --> 09:19.250
Just be patient.

09:23.040 --> 09:26.830
It's still remarkable that 
Sir Raphael's a butler now.

09:28.290 --> 09:31.460
Well... it's been a while 
since we've met, too.

09:35.860 --> 09:38.920
Forgive me. I've been a 
bit sleep-deprived lately.

09:42.500 --> 09:43.810
We're back!

09:46.160 --> 09:48.330
Miss Chastille! It's good to have you.

09:48.330 --> 09:50.020
Nephy! Welcome back!

09:50.600 --> 09:52.480
It's been a while, Chastille...

09:52.480 --> 09:53.740
Tail-Head.

09:53.740 --> 09:55.990
Why did you correct yourself?

09:55.990 --> 09:58.990
Well, thank you for having me over today.

09:58.990 --> 10:00.990
Hey. You seem to be doing well.

10:01.280 --> 10:02.240
Yeah.

10:02.240 --> 10:05.040
But I've been so busy, I haven't 
had time to go home lately.

10:05.560 --> 10:09.440
Cardinal Clavwell's death 
was declared an accident,

10:09.440 --> 10:14.090
which has led to me taking on nearly 
all his unfinished clerical work.

10:14.330 --> 10:15.460
I see.

10:19.150 --> 10:22.360
You realize, Barbatos, 
that you weren't invited?

10:22.360 --> 10:24.720
It wouldn't kill you to feed me, too!

10:24.720 --> 10:27.500
Do we have enough food for the minion?

10:28.190 --> 10:29.840
Hey, dragon shrimp!

10:29.840 --> 10:33.020
How many times do I gotta tell 
you I'm nobody's minion?!

10:33.560 --> 10:36.080
Watch your mouth.

10:36.080 --> 10:40.270
I don't have a lot of incentive to not kill 
you if you start insulting my daughter.

10:40.270 --> 10:43.030
But I've known you longer!

10:45.640 --> 10:49.050
Miss Chastille, Lord Barbatos, 
please, make yourselves at home.

10:49.050 --> 10:51.380
I'm going to prepare the meal.

10:51.380 --> 10:53.510
Oh, I'll help.

10:53.510 --> 10:55.090
That's all right. You must be tired.

10:55.090 --> 10:57.020
You're our guest today.

10:57.020 --> 10:59.420
It's fine. I want to help you.

10:59.810 --> 11:01.340
Thank you very much, then.

11:05.550 --> 11:07.600
Can you cook, Tail-Head?

11:07.900 --> 11:11.930
Yeah, not as well as Nephy, 
but I can handle most dishes.

11:11.930 --> 11:14.730
Now, what do you need me to do?

11:23.430 --> 11:25.870
The second she shows up, there's a ruckus.

11:25.870 --> 11:27.060
Let's see...

11:27.060 --> 11:28.220
There we go.

11:34.370 --> 11:35.910
Hey, Zagan...

11:35.910 --> 11:37.710
Are you still here?

11:37.710 --> 11:39.740
Don't touch anything.

11:39.740 --> 11:41.840
There are barriers up that 
could blow your arm off.

11:41.840 --> 11:43.700
I'm not that stupid!

11:43.700 --> 11:45.520
What the hell are you fiddling with there?

11:45.520 --> 11:49.140
Never seen one before?
 Granted, I hadn't, either.

11:49.140 --> 11:51.890
Fixing these kinds of things 
can be pretty interesting.

11:51.890 --> 11:55.460
Ancient sorcery can be simplistic, 
but very informative.

11:56.000 --> 11:57.860
You've got weird hobbies, y'know that?

11:57.860 --> 12:01.360
More importantly, you gotta do something 
about that knucklehead chick!

12:01.360 --> 12:03.030
She's gonna die at this rate!

12:03.030 --> 12:04.100
You mean Chastille?

12:04.100 --> 12:07.120
Are there are still people in 
the Church trying to kill her?

12:07.360 --> 12:09.560
This goes way beyond that!

12:09.560 --> 12:11.960
It's a whole comedy of errors 
with her, every damn night!

12:16.900 --> 12:18.210
There's still so much left.

12:18.670 --> 12:20.780
This is gonna take until morning.

12:23.700 --> 12:26.180
Okay, time for some tea!

12:31.190 --> 12:33.820
I had finally organized it...

12:35.440 --> 12:38.860
Ugh, this klutz! I can't bear to watch!

12:42.470 --> 12:43.830
Huh?

12:55.250 --> 12:57.650
I can't get a wink of sleep!

12:57.650 --> 13:01.600
At this rate, either she's 
gonna die or I will!

13:01.600 --> 13:03.590
I don't actually mind if you die.

13:04.270 --> 13:06.260
You don't?!

13:06.560 --> 13:09.600
Look, I'll treat you to 
all the drinks you want.

13:09.600 --> 13:11.360
You big jerk!

13:11.360 --> 13:12.390
Knock it off.

13:17.050 --> 13:19.960
Miss Chastille, how did the soup turn out?

13:19.960 --> 13:21.960
I think this should do it.

13:21.960 --> 13:23.790
Care to try, Nephy?

13:23.790 --> 13:24.400
Sure.

13:28.960 --> 13:30.080
Is something wrong?

13:32.790 --> 13:34.320
Is it that bad?

13:34.320 --> 13:37.320
It's worse than the muddy water 
I had to drink when I was young.

13:38.630 --> 13:41.500
Didn't she try it herself, though?

13:42.080 --> 13:44.170
This is a threat to our home's dinner table!

13:44.170 --> 13:45.510
I'll have to do something!

13:47.890 --> 13:50.600
L-Let's leave this right here for now!

13:50.880 --> 13:55.370
I'll... probably find a way to serve 
it with tomorrow's breakfast.

13:55.370 --> 13:58.940
So why don't you rest in your 
guest room, Miss Chastille?

13:58.940 --> 14:00.900
Find a way? But...

14:01.290 --> 14:04.530
Please don't steal my job. Okay?

14:08.830 --> 14:09.840
Is it fixed?

14:09.840 --> 14:10.530
Yeah.

14:20.490 --> 14:22.320
That's lovely music.

14:22.320 --> 14:23.500
It really is.

14:23.760 --> 14:26.310
Yes. The interesting part 
of this device is that

14:26.310 --> 14:29.050
you can choose different songs 
depending on the occasion.

14:29.440 --> 14:30.840
Good atmosphere.

14:31.120 --> 14:34.040
Classy in a way that doesn't suit an
 Archdemon's dinner party, I'd say.

14:34.040 --> 14:39.730
I believe I once visited a dance hall 
in a port town that had one of these.

14:40.120 --> 14:41.270
A dance hall?

14:41.550 --> 14:47.490
The ladies and gentlemen danced hand-in-hand
to the music from the phonograph.

14:47.800 --> 14:51.160
Really? You're pretty worldly.

14:51.450 --> 14:53.980
But then, the sorcerers present attacked me,

14:53.980 --> 14:56.450
which led to me being banned 
from the premises.

14:58.580 --> 15:00.710
Now then, everyone, please be seated.

15:02.420 --> 15:04.170
Time to eat.

15:04.450 --> 15:08.200
Wow, Nephy's cooking is as good as ever.

15:08.200 --> 15:12.090
It's so refreshingly fragrant, 
with a complex flavor profile.

15:14.260 --> 15:18.270
What the hell does a knucklehead
 like you know about complex flavors?!

15:18.580 --> 15:21.900
I don't see where you get 
off making that criticism.

15:23.380 --> 15:26.690
If you don't like it, maybe grow up enough 
to stop sleeping with a stuffed animal!

15:28.070 --> 15:30.650
H-How do you know about Poco?!

15:31.060 --> 15:32.160
Poco?!

15:33.450 --> 15:35.890
Are you drunk already?!

15:35.890 --> 15:38.700
Forgive me. He said you 
gave him permission.

15:38.790 --> 15:40.290
<b>Empty</b>

15:39.130 --> 15:40.290
The whole bottle?!

15:41.570 --> 15:45.290
W-Wait, have you been peeping 
on me from the shadows?!

15:47.410 --> 15:49.860
Why would anyone wanna peep 
on you of all people?!

15:49.860 --> 15:52.800
I'm not a babysitter, dammit! 
Why am I stuck watching out for you?!

15:55.710 --> 15:57.810
I don't recall you looking out for me!

15:58.120 --> 16:02.060
Oh, Chastille, he's just drunk. 
Pay him no mind.

16:02.060 --> 16:05.310
<i>The way things are going, I definitely
 can't tell her that he's been guarding her.</i>

16:05.620 --> 16:07.330
Oh, Miss Chastille?

16:07.330 --> 16:09.400
When you collapsed from the poison,

16:09.400 --> 16:12.200
it was Lord Barbatos who brought you here.

16:12.760 --> 16:15.160
<i>Nicely done, Nephy! Good save.</i>

16:15.440 --> 16:17.410
Wait, really?

16:17.410 --> 16:21.350
I-I see. I don't really 
remember what happened.

16:21.350 --> 16:23.830
I appreciate what you did. Thank you.

16:23.830 --> 16:27.710
Save the thanks until after 
you've grown into a finer woman!

16:27.710 --> 16:28.710
<b>Huh?!</b>

16:28.990 --> 16:34.370
My ideal woman is someone older and 
open-minded who'll spoil me rotten!

16:34.370 --> 16:36.640
No one asked!

16:37.130 --> 16:40.770
I notice you never actually 
denied peeping on me.

16:41.510 --> 16:43.900
And then you revealed Poco's existence...

16:45.620 --> 16:47.720
P-Please don't cry!

16:48.900 --> 16:50.820
It must've broken down.

16:50.820 --> 16:52.860
No fighting during meals!

16:55.680 --> 16:57.440
For's right.

16:57.440 --> 16:59.870
Barbatos, you're at fault here. Apologize.

17:00.360 --> 17:01.400
Hell no!

17:04.650 --> 17:08.500
Hey, this soup tastes wild! 
The bitterness is real strong.

17:08.500 --> 17:09.790
I think I could get used to it!

17:10.080 --> 17:13.830
Soup? I didn't serve any soup.

17:14.350 --> 17:16.750
That's the one that Tail-Head made.

17:16.750 --> 17:18.680
I put it out for the minion.

17:18.680 --> 17:19.800
You did?!

17:20.180 --> 17:24.390
A-Are you alright Lord Barbatos? 
Do you feel strange at all?

17:24.730 --> 17:25.640
<b>Huh?</b>

17:29.000 --> 17:30.190
Lord Barbatos!

17:30.470 --> 17:34.490
Nephy! Was the soup I made really that bad?!

17:35.020 --> 17:37.660
Uh, well, that's...

17:37.980 --> 17:39.520
Quit crying, Tail-Head!

17:39.520 --> 17:40.660
Miss Chastille...

17:41.050 --> 17:42.540
Why?! Why?!

17:46.720 --> 17:48.630
Nephy, seconds...

17:57.380 --> 17:59.770
Nephy? You must be tired.

18:00.740 --> 18:01.640
A bit.

18:02.130 --> 18:04.020
But I had a good time.

18:04.020 --> 18:07.310
I've never had a meal with 
such a large group before.

18:07.310 --> 18:10.860
And everyone ate so much.

18:10.860 --> 18:13.290
The power of good food 
shouldn't be trifled with.

18:14.600 --> 18:18.620
Lord Zagan, why did you buy that phonograph?

18:19.470 --> 18:23.990
Just a whim, but... I also 
wanted you to enjoy some music.

18:24.350 --> 18:25.950
Thank you.

18:26.600 --> 18:28.250
Just wait a bit. It's almost fixed.

18:28.790 --> 18:33.640
Lord Zagan, when you reminisce about the past, 
 you always look so sad.

18:33.640 --> 18:36.320
But today seemed different.

18:36.320 --> 18:37.510
Did it?

18:39.330 --> 18:42.010
I'm not sure, but when 
I lived on the street,

18:42.010 --> 18:44.030
I didn't have a home or a 
regular source of food,

18:44.030 --> 18:46.020
but I did have friends to share bread with.

18:46.500 --> 18:50.900
<i>Maybe back then, I was less 
lonely than I thought.</i>

18:51.430 --> 18:53.270
<i>And I'm only now realizing...</i>

18:53.270 --> 18:56.280
<i>Ever since I shut myself in this castle,
 I've never gone back.</i>

18:56.280 --> 18:58.780
<i>I wonder if anyone I knew is still around.</i>

18:59.350 --> 19:01.780
<i>I hope they all managed to survive.</i>

19:02.230 --> 19:03.340
Say, Nephy...

19:03.340 --> 19:04.400
Yes?

19:04.400 --> 19:06.730
Would you mind if I returned 
this to the streets?

19:08.290 --> 19:09.330
Not at all.

19:23.040 --> 19:26.060
<i>I had no idea that singing 
could sound so beautiful.</i>

19:28.290 --> 19:31.810
<i>It's the same shock I felt the 
first time I heard Nephy's voice.</i>

19:32.300 --> 19:34.240
Nephy... shall we dance?

19:35.300 --> 19:37.780
<i>I only meant to say that 
her singing was nice!</i>

19:38.400 --> 19:39.280
Yes.

19:39.510 --> 19:40.900
<i>Y-Yes?!</i>

19:41.300 --> 19:42.540
O-Okay.

19:50.380 --> 19:53.000
<i>How does... one dance?</i>

20:00.230 --> 20:04.010
My lord, I can instruct you 
on the necessary steps.

20:06.230 --> 20:10.630
<i>In the deep, deep forest 
known as the Lost Woods,</i>

20:11.380 --> 20:15.360
<i>a man who was once alone, was not any longer.</i>

20:17.260 --> 20:21.240
My lord, you need to actually 
move for it to be practice.

20:24.590 --> 20:26.330
They're such a handful.

20:29.740 --> 20:30.970
<i>The next day...</i>

20:30.970 --> 20:35.340
<i>The citizens of Kianoides 
experienced a shock.</i>

20:35.970 --> 20:38.460
<i>Music was playing from a back alley,</i>

20:38.460 --> 20:41.210
<i>with children happily dancing to it.</i>

20:42.090 --> 20:47.140
<i>It was like a spontaneous 
festival that lasted all day.</i>

20:57.450 --> 21:01.570
<i>But now, let's roll time 
back to this evening.</i>

21:02.000 --> 21:05.830
<i>The night that the two of them danced 
together for the first time.</i>

21:06.750 --> 21:07.910
<i>His name is Zagan.</i>

21:09.040 --> 21:10.660
<i>Her name is Nephy.</i>

21:11.340 --> 21:16.600
<i>And their very, very long 
story has only just begun.</i>

21:25.510 --> 21:27.760
I wouldn't mind staying like this.

21:28.160 --> 21:31.010
That's no fair, Lord Zagan.
